2Dpolicy\\\\\\u0022\\u0020target\\u003D\\\\\\u0022_blank\\\\\\u0022\\u003EPrivacy\\u0020Notice\\u003C\\\\\\/a\\u003E.\\u0020You\\u0020also\\u0020agree\\u0020to\\u0020receive\\u0020marketing\\u0020emails\\u0020from\\u0020us\\u0020that\\u0020may\\u0020include\\u0020promotions\\u0020from\\u0020our\\u0020trusted\\u0020partners\\u0020and\\u0020sponsors,\\u0020which\\u0020you\\u0020can\\u0020unsubscribe\\u0020from\\u0020at\\u0020any\\u0020time.\\u0022'\n)\">\n<p>Sign up for breaking news, reviews, opinion, top tech deals, and more.</p>\n\n\n\n</section>\n</div>\n\n\n<div data-component-name=\"Slice:AuthorBio\" id=\"slice-container-authorBio-EggnX7YwBkDbGTaSdx53iR\" data-author-bio-max-height=\"250\" data-author-bio-read-more=\"Read more\" data-author-bio-read-less=\"Read less\"><p>Contributor </p><p>Writer, broadcaster, musician and kitchen gadget obsessive Carrie Marshall has been writing about tech since 1998, contributing sage advice and odd opinions to all kinds of magazines and websites as well as writing more than twenty books. Her latest, a love letter to music titled <a href=\"https://www.404ink.com/store/p/small-town-joy-carrie-marshall\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">Small Town Joy</a>, is on sale now. She is the singer in spectacularly obscure Glaswegian rock band <a href=\"http://unquietmindmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">Unquiet Mind</a>.</p></div>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></DIV>","content_text":"(Image credit: Future) The TCL QM7L is the best mid-range TV of 2026, and right now you can get the 65-inch version with a whopping 43% price reduction: where the TCL QM7L was $1,499.99 it is now just $847.99 at Amazon. At full price the TV was a great buy. At this price it's a doorbuster, the kind of saving you'd queue up for.• Browse the full Amazon Black Friday saleIn our in-depth TCL QM7L review we gave it 4.5 out of five stars, praising its picture quality, its gamer-friendly features (including a high refresh rate and AMD Freesync Pro) and its excellent value for money.As our expert reviewer James Holland explained, the TCL QM7L is \"impressive with up to 2,100 local dimming zones, up to 3,000 nits at peak brightness, TCL’s anti-halo and color enhancing tech, and AI features such as the imperfect generative voice assistant in Google Gemini. The sound is still provided by Bang & Olufsen and the refresh rate (and passthrough from HDMI ports) is high enough that it will make for one of the best gaming TVs for those trying to strike a balance between premium performance and price.\"We'd quibble very slightly with Amazon's RRP here — Amazon says $1,499, but the 65-inch launch price was $1,299 — but this is still a substantial saving on a very good mid-range television that takes the price well into bargain territory.Today's best TCL QM7L dealMore Black Friday deals in the USAmazon: up to 65% off tech & essentialsBest Buy: up to 50% off TVs, laptops & appliancesDell: up to $700 off laptopsHome Depot: 50% off appliances, grills & toolsLenovo: up to 50% off laptopsLowe's: up to 30% off appliances & holiday decorSamsung: up to $1,000 off TVs & phonesT-Mobile: free iPhone or Galaxy with a planTarget: Christmas decor & gifts from $7.99Walmart: early access to deals for members Get daily insight, inspiration and deals in your inbox Sign up for breaking news, reviews, opinion, top tech deals, and more. Contributor Writer, broadcaster, musician and kitchen gadget obsessive Carrie Marshall has been writing about tech since 1998, contributing sage advice and odd opinions to all kinds of magazines and websites as well as writing more than twenty books. Her latest, a love letter to music titled Small Town Joy, is on sale now. She is the singer in spectacularly obscure Glaswegian rock band Unquiet Mind.","fetched_at":"2026-11-27T15:38:11.325Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<figcaption> <span>(Image credit: Future)</span>\n</figcaption>","sentences":[{"en":"(Image credit: Future)","zh":"（图片来源：未来）"}]},{"html_en":"<p id